                       What each honesty constraint costs                       
┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━┳━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┳━━━━━━━━┳━━━━━━━━━━━┳━━━━━━━━━━━━┓
┃ variant     ┃ what it assumes              ┃ PR-AUC ┃ vs honest ┃   Rs saved ┃
┡━━━━━━━━━━━━━╇━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╇━━━━━━━━╇━━━━━━━━━━━╇━━━━━━━━━━━━┩
│ honest      │ causal features, 30d         │ 0.5986 │         - │ 18,476,797 │
│             │ reporting lag (shipped)      │        │           │            │
│ lag0        │ chargebacks known instantly  │ 0.9691 │    +61.9% │ 52,814,554 │
│             │ (impossible)                 │        │           │            │
│ whole_frame │ ring aggregates over the     │ 0.9612 │    +60.6% │ 52,264,200 │
│             │ whole dataset (classic leak) │        │           │            │
└─────────────┴──────────────────────────────┴────────┴───────────┴────────────┘

Reading this table. A variant scoring above `honest` is not better -- it is the 
amount by which a submission making that standard mistake would overstate 
itself. A variant scoring BELOW honest means the shortcut also cost it something
real, and the comparison is confounded rather than clean.
